  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Revenue contraction points to soft demand in core small appliance categories, partially counterbalanced by strong double-digit growth in the health segment, indicating some diversification success. Gross margin expanded meaningfully from favorable pricing and mix, though roughly two-fifths of the gain came from a one-time tariff-related inventory sell-through, introducing sustainability questions. The uncertain tariff refund situation and tepid end-market conditions keep the top-line outlook subdued despite the sharp profitability improvement.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership chose to protect margins over volume, leveraging a foreign trade zone and pricing actions to lift operating profit even as sales fell. They reiterated full-year guidance, signaling confidence, and returned cash through a modest quarterly dividend increase, reinforcing a shareholder-friendly posture. However, reliance on a transitory tariff benefit to deliver the earnings beat, coupled with unresolved IEEPA refund risks, tempers the credibility of the margin narrative and raises flags about the durability of recent profit gains.",
